      "card_ids": ["C88","C103","C111","C116"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L1 direct oral bioavailability values for structurally related N-acylpiperazine/heteroaryl amine or dimethoxy-substituted scaffolds are all >=23%: delavirdine 85% (C16/C19/C25), suvorexant 82% (C23), GSK1322322 57% fasted (C29), valbenazine ~49% (C03), brigatinib 46% (C28), donepezil ~100% (C04/C06), piritrexim ~75% (C14/C22), metoclopramide 79-82% (C15/C18); other piritrexim patient F values are 40-63% (C01/C10/C24/C27), and the lowest direct value is 23% (C13), still above threshold.",
      "card_ids": ["C16","C19","C25","C23","C29","C03","C28","C04","C06","C14","C22","C15","C18","C13","C01","C10","C24","C27"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 species/formulation records remain consistent with F >=20%: donepezil dog F 28.4% (C52) and rat F 41.4% (C64), valbenazine dog F 74.1% (C45), brigatinib rat F 52% (C51), delavirdine >80% (C65), metoclopramide 82% (C67), and multiple human donepezil values near 100% (C31/C35/C71/C72).",
      "card_ids": ["C52","C64","C45","C51","C65","C67","C31","C35","C71","C72"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The single qualitative 'low bioavailability' statement for a marketed donepezil formulation (C33) is outweighed by multiple human donepezil F values near 100% and is not transferable to the query; it does not constitute affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for F <20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C33","C04","C06","C31","C35","C71","C72"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The physicochemical prior is favorable (MW 383 Da, logD 1.69, HBD 1, TPSA 107 Å², 4 rotatable bonds, 81% neutral at pH 7.4), with no strong liability indicating F <20%.",
      "card_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C88","C103","C111","C116"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability or matched oral/IV exposure record for the query molecule itself is present in the supplied cards; support is from structurally related contexts, chiefly the tetrahydrofuran analog terazosin (M02).",
    "L3 terazosin records provide Cmax/tmax but lack dose, formulation, and IV comparator, so they cannot independently quantify F.",
    "No direct solubility, permeability, or first-pass metabolism measurements for the query are supplied; furan and aniline moieties are potential metabolic liabilities but are not quantified.",
    "Most L3 records concern unrelated scaffolds (olaparib, trimethoprim, bosutinib, etc.) and were not used."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: F >=20% remains well supported. L1 direct F values for related N-acylpiperazine/dimethoxy-substituted scaffolds range from 23% to ~100%; L2 species/formulation records are consistent; L3 adds human oral Cmax/tmax for the close analog terazosin (M02), confirming measurable oral exposure. No affirmative threshold-relevant evidence supports F <20%."
}

